        <groundspeak:log id="681708683">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-28T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1095439">GeoGuider</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP598 Riverdale School 2017 04 27&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posted:     N 53° 32.619 W 113° 28.102&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;My GPSr:  N 53° 32.621 W 113° 28.108&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I met j0ckser as he was getting off from work and we travelled in tandem here.  What an interesting story about the teacher who taught here.  I can’t imagine teaching for 65 of her 81 years. I can’t imagine starting teaching when I was 16 either, much less teaching till I die. (Mind you there ARE days, but nothing that a nice glass of wine or Crown and coke won’t cure! LOL) This was a much easier find than the ones we were looking for yesterday.  The cap itself has been painted… twice. Thanks for the cap OTFH.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681182441">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP598 Riverdale School

Grabbed a couple more BCPs today on the way to home. Quick find but the cap was unreadable. I remember come down here as a kid with my grandparents to go the the greenhouse. Then it felt like going back in time. The neighbourhood has certainly turned out nice. 

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="650873871">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-11-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3854161">Stonagal</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP598 - Riverdale School

Found the cap, but it's been beaten up pretty bad and is no longer legible. Even the words around the edge are impossible to decipher. Sent the CO a photo and received permission to log. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
